[stderr] +## GD0002 editorial acceptance register
[stderr] +
[stderr] +[`qba-editorial-acceptance-register.json`](qba-editorial-acceptance-register.json)
[stderr] +is the durable, machine-readable ledger for all existing `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-48`
[stderr] +revision-1 records. It intentionally records no fictional acceptance: every
[stderr] +record is individually listed with its existing batch and source-family route,
[stderr] +and inherits five explicit pending reasons for un-authored original expression,
[stderr] +missing resolvable provenance, each distinct review, and the incomplete release
[stderr] +transition. Its `selectionEligible: false` default is a hard audit assertion,
[stderr] +not a future promise; a selector must reject every record until current-revision
[stderr] +evidence replaces every pending item and the lifecycle reaches `published`.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The register's `batches`, `records`, and `validation` fields make the finite
[stderr] +boundary inspectable without changing it: exactly four named batches, exactly
[stderr] +12 IDs in each, exactly 48 unique IDs matching `QB-A-01…48`, and no extra
[stderr] +record. A future editor must add card-specific evidence rather than changing a
[stderr] +default or accepting the manifest; a blocked, rejected, conflicted, withdrawn,
[stderr] +or still-pending revision remains `selectionEligible: false` with its reason.
