.md-112-optional replacement. It does not silently replace cards or rewrite past rounds.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:113:New selection excludes it from that time; a presented attempt resolves against\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:114:its presented revision. Only a corrected, newly reviewed revision may publish.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-115-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-116-## Seeded anti-repeat and shortage policy\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-117-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-118-For `(catalogueSnapshotId, seed, requestedCount, filter, ledger)`, freeze the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:119:published eligible catalogue at the snapshot, apply filter, then remove\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-120-blocked/withdrawn cards. `recent` is the union of IDs in the two latest\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-121-*completed* rounds, sorting rounds by `(completedAtUtc, roundId)` descending.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-122-Draft, abandoned, and in-progress rounds do not count.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-123-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-125-`SHA-256(seed + \"|\" + catalogueSnapshotId + \"|\" + cardId)`, then sort\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-126-ascending by `(key, cardId)`. Take the first\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-127-`min(requestedCount, fresh.length)`; fill only the remainder from\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-128-`reuse = candidates \u2229 recent` in the same order. Whenever reuse occurs or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:129:eligible cards are too few, record:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-130-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:131:`{ requestedCount, freshAvailable, eligibleAvailable, reusedCardIds,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:132:unfilledCount, disclosureKey: \"selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed\" }`.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-133-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-134-Show this plain-language disclosure before round start whenever reuse or an\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-135-unfilled count exists. No clock, random source, network response, unpublished\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:136:card, or iteration order affects selection. Equal full input has equal IDs and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-137-shortage record.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-138-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:139:### Eight seeded selection fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-140-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-141-Candidate lists are frozen, filtered, and published; R1/R2 are newest completed\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-142-rounds. Implementation fixtures calculate the specified SHA-256 ordering and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-143-assert selected IDs, shortage fields, and disclosure key.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-155-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-156-## Release checks\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-157-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-158-Eligibility requires published frozen-snapshot state, correct answer rule, no\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:159:alias collision, current provenance, two distinct accepted reviews, and no\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-160-effective withdrawal. The fixture suite requires exactly ADJ-01\u2013ADJ-20 and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-161-SEL-01\u2013SEL-08. Failed validation blocks release; it cannot create a fallback\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-162-answer or undisclosed repeat.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-6-the records that pass the release gate in this document.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-7-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-8-## Release boundary and original-expression rule\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-9-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:10:`QB-A` (\"Kickoff Mix\") is exactly the 48 stable IDs `QB-A-01` through\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:11:`QB-A-48`, divided into four named 12-card batches. The IDs are permanent:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-12-a correction increments the revision and preserves the ID; a withdrawn card is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:13:not silently replaced. No other `QB-A-*` ID is in the first release.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-14-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-15-The catalogue's question intents and canonical answers below are authored for\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-16-this game. At production, the copy editor writes a fresh, concise prompt and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-17-explanation from the stated facts; authors must not reproduce source wording,\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-27-rules (the detailed normalisation policy is owned by `GPI-006`).\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-28-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-29-| Field | Rule / purpose |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-30-| --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:31:| `id`, `revision`, `batchId`, `status` | Stable ID, positive revision, one named batch, and lifecycle: `draft \u2192 fact_checked \u2192 accessibility_edited \u2192 second_reviewed \u2192 published`; alternatively `blocked` or `withdrawn`. Only `published` is eligible. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-32-| `originalityRecord` | Author ID/creation date, independently-authored confirmation, and a non-copying check. It records inspiration boundaries, never reference-product text. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-33-| `promptKey`, `promptText`, `instructionKey` | One independently written, single-fact prompt plus a format-appropriate, plain-language instruction. Prompt text must be answerable without an image, sound, colour, time limit, or unstated context. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-34-| `format` | Exactly one of `four_option_select`, `true_false`, `ordered_pair`, or `short_typed_answer`. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-35-| `category`, `topic`, `era`, `competitionScopes`, `clubIds`, `difficultyBand`, `tags` | Discovery and quota fields. `difficultyBand` is integer 1\u20133; all material competition/club references must be listed to enforce caps. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:36:| `answerOptions` | Required only for select/true-false. Select has exactly four unique option IDs and one `correct`; true/false has canonical `true`/`false` IDs. Options are text-labelled and have non-colour selection/result states. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-37-| `canonicalAnswer` and `acceptedAnswerRule` | Select/true-false use canonical option IDs; ordered pair specifies exactly two ordered canonical IDs; typed answer provides canonical display answer, normalised accepted aliases, and no fuzzy match. Empty aliases and aliases that could mean another answer are invalid. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-38-| `explanationKey`, `explanationText` | Short fact-first explanation shown after resolution, including canonical answer where useful. It must explain why rather than merely say \"correct\". |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:39:| `accessibility` | `screenReaderPrompt`, `screenReaderOptions` where applicable, `answerStateText`, `explanationTextEquivalent`, reading-order/focus requirement, and text-size/contrast review. No visual or audio-only clue may be needed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-40-| `provenanceId`, `factualAssertions[]` | Links each assertion to permitted durable sources/research records, source locator, checked date, and conflict/correction history. All assertions must be supported. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:41:| `reviews[]` | Two distinct completed reviews: factual/rights review and accessibility/copy review. Each carries reviewer ID/role, decision, date, findings, and revision reviewed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-42-| `localeKeys`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `withdrawal` | Externalised player strings and audit timestamps. Withdrawal requires reason, effective date, and replacement relationship only when one exists. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-43-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-44-**Format accessibility rules.** Four-option select renders every option as a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-45-labelled button and never uses position as the only clue. True/false spells out\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-46-both values. Ordered pair labels first/second positions and supports reorder by\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-47-keyboard and touch. Typed answer announces validation requirements, preserves\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-48-entered text on rejected submission, and always exposes the canonical answer\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-49-and explanation after resolution. Every format supports touch, pointer,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:50:keyboard, and gamepad-equivalent selection; no format relies on a timer.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-51-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:52:## Provenance and two-review workflow\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-53-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-54-Each inventory row references a source family below; the eventual card's\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-55-`provenanceId` is `PROV-<card ID>` and must contain the precise page/document\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-56-URL, retrieval date, factual-assertion mapping, and correction log before it\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-69-| `DFL` / `LFP` | DFL Bundesliga and Ligue de Football Professionnel official history/competition records |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-70-| `FF` | France Football's official Ballon d'Or records |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-71-| `CLUB` | The relevant club's official history/records page, cross-checked against its competition organiser where the assertion concerns a competition |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-72-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:73:For each card revision, reviewer `R1` (factual/rights editor) verifies every\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-74-assertion against the exact provenance locator, source permission and original\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-75-expression record. Reviewer `R2` (accessibility/copy editor), a different\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-76-person, verifies unambiguous language, answer options/aliases, explanation,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-77-screen-reader text, non-colour state wording, and localisation keys. R1's\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-78-accepted decision moves the record to `fact_checked`; R2's accepted decision\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:79:moves it to `second_reviewed`; only the release editor may then set\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-80-`published`. A rejection or later dispute sets `blocked`; a published error\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:81:sets `withdrawn` until both reviews approve a new revision. Reviewer identity,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-82-date, revision, decision, and finding are mandatory, making absent or duplicate\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:83:reviews mechanically rejectable.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-84-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:85:## `GPI-002`\u2013`GPI-005`: bounded batch inventory\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-86-\nprojects/football-